GUI derivatives include ClickGui/Category/Module, Settings/InnerSettingsScreen,
FlatTextbox, PlainLabel, ToggleButton, KeybindButton and Rendering.drawBorder.
Changed for solyanka: Kotlin port, Minecraft 26.2 screen/navigation APIs,
solyanka module adapter, staged/validated command-profile editors, typed input
device capture, known-feature-only catalog and explicit screen cleanup.
The original NoFrills module/config/event runtime is not bundled.
See docs/GUI_PORT.md and docs/M1.md for source paths and behavior differences.

Command adaptations retain typed persistence, device separation, focus guards,
conservative context filters, live aliases and cycle/length checks.

owo-lib (MIT), Mod Menu (MIT), Fabric and Fabric Language Kotlin are separate
external runtime dependencies, not bundled into this mod JAR. YACL is no
longer a solyanka dependency as of 0.2.1.
Gradle wrapper bootstrap files originate from FabricMC/fabric-example-mod (CC0).
Remaining requested upstream gameplay/render implementations and artwork are
not included yet; see the feature matrix for the exact implemented subset.

0.3.0 derivatives additionally include features/general/ChatTweaks.java,
features/general/InfoTooltips.java, mixin/ChatComponentMixin.java,
mixin/GuiMixin.java (disconnect chat operation), misc/Utils.java (plain text,
market item IDs and local dates), misc/ShardData.java (shard identification and
alias mapping), and the museum-cache concept in misc/NoFrillsAPI.java.
Changed: Kotlin/26.2 hooks, parent-message copying, staged typed settings,
malformed-data handling, bounded background HTTP and public Hypixel resource
provider in place of the inaccessible NoFrills museum endpoint. See docs/M2.md.
No Hypixel resource response or game assets are bundled. Endec 0.1.12 (MIT)
is compile-only; its runtime copy is already bundled within external owo.

0.3.1 UI changes: same-Screen embedded settings adapters, isolated modal input,
immediate validated persistence and inline failure status replace the previous
staged save/navigation flow. Original NoFrills attribution remains applicable.

